<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n49536" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θύρσος</span></b> , ὁ, in late
		Poets with heterocl. pl. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θύρσα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					6.158
				</span></i>
			 (Sabin.): —<i>wand wreathed in ivy and vine-leaves
				with a pine-cone at the top</i>, carried by the devotees of
			Dionysus, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Ba.</u>
				80
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				1109.138
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hero
				<u>Spir.</u>
				2.9
			</span></i>, etc.; also of the <i>devotees</i> themselves, Sch.<i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Hec.</u>
				261
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κλάδος, ῥάβδος</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i> (Prob. a loan-word.)</div>
